(7734776, 1274801, 103142, '<td valign="top">OMG!! Good to see you! Still one of my all time favorite photographers! Congrats on the top 10 and hope to see you around a lot more!</td>', 'OMG!! Good to see you! Still one of my all time favorite photographers! Congrats on the top 10 and hope to see you around a lot more!', '2022-12-16 15:34:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(7734778, 1274801, 7810, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by vawendy:</b></div><hr/><i> OMG!! Good to see you! Still one of my all time favorite photographers! Congrats on the top 10 and hope to see you around a lot more! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi Wendy :D  Thanks so much for the kind words. Your comment made my hat feel a little tighter LOL.  I hope to participate more often. DP has always been a great place to charge the creative juices.<br/>Thanks again !!!</td>', 'Originally posted by vawendy: OMG!! Good to see you! Still one of my all time favorite photographers! Congrats on the top 10 and hope to see you around a lot more!   Hi Wendy :D  Thanks so much for the kind words. Your comment made my hat feel a little tighter LOL.  I hope to participate more often. DP has always been a great place to charge the creative juices.Thanks again !!!', '2022-12-16 15:41:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(7734799, 1274745, 97225, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous horses, gorgeous photo. Congrats on the blue, Roz.</td>', 'Gorgeous horses, gorgeous photo. Congrats on the blue, Roz.', '2022-12-16 20:06:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(7734800, 1274756, 97225, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the ribbon, Anita. Beautiful, characteristically Aussie photo, lovely tones and light. Nothing wrong with angles. Trees lean! The fence posts are straight, the sheep are upright, which shows that the camera was straight. I don''t see any overall tilt to the left, but why do people assume that ground should be level? (Except when it''s covered with concrete.)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2022-12-16 20:29:57.</i></td>', 'Congrats on the ribbon, Anita. Beautiful, characteristically Aussie photo, lovely tones and light. Nothing wrong with angles. Trees lean! The fence posts are straight, the sheep are upright, which shows that the camera was straight. I don''t see any overall tilt to the left, but why do people assume that ground should be level? (Except when it''s covered with concrete.)', '2022-12-16 20:26:08.000000', '2022-12-16 20:29:57.000000', 0),
(7734805, 1274745, 42013, '<td valign="top">so beautiful Roz. You have eye contact with the lead horse.</td>', 'so beautiful Roz. You have eye contact with the lead horse.', '2022-12-16 23:34:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(7734812, 1274831, 114285, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by MeMex2:</b></div><hr/><i> Anita..it was on a ramshackle, mess of a farm on the outskirts of Sarasota, Florida.<br/>These guys were in a field and someone must have called them in for food. When I got out of the car<br/>they looked straight at me..problem was my lens was not long enough and the quality was awful. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for the explanation, I absolutely loved the noise reduction, it really made this image special imho. After all arent most animals soft and cuddly :)</td>', 'Originally posted by MeMex2: Anita..it was on a ramshackle, mess of a farm on the outskirts of Sarasota, Florida.These guys were in a field and someone must have called them in for food. When I got out of the carthey looked straight at me..problem was my lens was not long enough and the quality was awful.   Thanks for the explanation, I absolutely loved the noise reduction, it really made this image special imho. After all arent most animals soft and cuddly :)', '2022-12-17 09:30:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(7734840, 1274756, 67145, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by roz:</b></div><hr/><i> such a great image Anita .. definitely a character shot .. :)<br/>had the neat stamp for sure .. sheep for one .. lol .. and one of your trademark tones .. you have a couple/few .. trademark tones that is .. <br/>i loved that the sheep are all looking at you .. and actually standing still .. did you hypnotize them haha .. ;)<br/> <br/>and its interesting how we all view things differently .. i didnt find anything odd about the angles at all .. especially as we have trees here that are leaning because of the prevailing winds .. often one will be leaning and one quite close wont be .. not sure why that is .. :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes the trees if they are not staked early then its too late A real pet hate of mine. Ive actually pulled out trees from my garden if they end up like that, I cant stand it, the perfectionist in me LOL. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>re the perfectionist in you .. <br/>that makes two of us lol .. ;)<br/>although for me it doesn''t extend to my ''garden'' .. <br/>editing however .. that''s another story .. not sure if it''s a sad or happy story though .. xx</td>', 'Originally posted by Neat: Originally posted by roz: such a great image Anita .. definitely a character shot .. :)had the neat stamp for sure .. sheep for one .. lol .. and one of your trademark tones .. you have a couple/few .. trademark tones that is .. i loved that the sheep are all looking at you .. and actually standing still .. did you hypnotize them haha .. ;) and its interesting how we all view things differently .. i didnt find anything odd about the angles at all .. especially as we have trees here that are leaning because of the prevailing winds .. often one will be leaning and one quite close wont be .. not sure why that is .. :)   Yes the trees if they are not staked early then its too late A real pet hate of mine. Ive actually pulled out trees from my garden if they end up like that, I cant stand it, the perfectionist in me LOL.   re the perfectionist in you .. that makes two of us lol .. ;)although for me it doesn''t extend to my ''garden'' .. editing however .. that''s another story .. not sure if it''s a sad or happy story though .. xx', '2022-12-17 19:59:18.000000', NULL, 0),
